Next, subtract the number of eggs used from the total number of eggs laid:
\[ 16 \text{ eggs} - 7 \text{ eggs} = 9 \text{ eggs} \]

Finally, calculate the revenue from selling the remaining eggs:
\[ 9 \text{ eggs} \times 2 \text{ dollars/egg} = 18 \text{ dollars} \]

Therefore, Janet makes $18 every day at the farmers' market.

